   "id": 3514843,
   "postDate": "2026-08-20T08:43:23.920Z",
   "rawMarkdown": "![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-forum-message-attachments/o/inbox%2F9945255%2F1e0c3afa532c28ab127ee7e06f056c80%2Fgorilla-d847cd71000730cd511a3f5f355bf95654ead0ca.webp?generation=1787215357782115&alt=media)\n\nThe image above is a CT scan. This image contains a gorilla. According to this article, even highly trained radiologists often miss the gorilla.\n\nBefore blindly training models with Coding Agent, it might be a good idea to check if there is a gorilla in the knee MRI.\n\nhttps://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2013/02/11/171409656/why-even-radiologists-can-miss-a-gorilla-hiding-in-plain-sight",
   "content": "<p><img src=\"https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-forum-message-attachments/o/inbox%2F9945255%2F1e0c3afa532c28ab127ee7e06f056c80%2Fgorilla-d847cd71000730cd511a3f5f355bf95654ead0ca.webp?generation=1787215357782115&amp;alt=media\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p>The image above is a CT scan. This image contains a gorilla. According to this article, even highly trained radiologists often miss the gorilla.</p>\n<p>Before blindly training models with Coding Agent, it might be a good idea to check if there is a gorilla in the knee MRI.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2013/02/11/171409656/why-even-radiologists-can-miss-a-gorilla-hiding-in-plain-sight\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2013/02/11/171409656/why-even-radiologists-can-miss-a-gorilla-hiding-in-plain-sight</a></p>",
